{
  "decision": "include",
  "confidence": 1.0,
  "reason": "The study reports a quantitative comparison of radiation carcinogenesis between humans and mice using a mathematical model. It provides specific quantitative measures of agreement and differences, such as the 'time shift per dose' (7.8 years per Gy for humans vs. 0.046 years per Gy for mice) and the effect per dose on a per-lifespan basis (0.72-fold for humans vs. 0.71-fold for mice). This directly addresses the criteria for including records that report quantitative measures of agreement or comparison of effect sizes between animal and human results."
}
